      "cup-pskill": {
       "cup-options": {
        "durationFormat": "seconds",
        "helpText": "<p>Have you ever wondered what it's like to go camping without a tent? I took a survival camping course last summer, and I learned a lot. The first thing we learned was how to find water. Surprisingly, we could do this by looking for very green, healthy plants. This shows that there is water nearby. After we found a river, we went fishing to catch our dinner. Predictably, it was quite hard as we were trying to fish in an area that had no fish! Afterwards, we learned how to make a fire. Amazingly, even though we hadn't found any dry leaves or small branches, it was really easy! Then, we found places to sleep. It's safer to sleep near other people to keep animals away. By this stage, I was pretty tired, so I fell asleep very easily. All in all, I enjoyed the experience, and I undoubtedly learned a lot. But I was also very happy to go home the next morning!<br></p>",
        "helpTitle": "Example",
        "instructions": "Write a short article about an unexpected experience you had. What happened? What was your opinion of it?<br>&nbsp;<br>Here are some ideas:<br><ul><li>Begin the article with a direct question to get the reader's attention.</li><li>Use a sequence of events, or compare and contrast ideas.</li><li>Use comment adverbs.</li><li>Use linking words.</li><li>Summarise your experience or ideas and evaluate them.</li></ul>Useful language:<br>amazingly<br>naturally<br>inevitably<br>(not) surprisingly<br>predictably<br>undoubtedly<br>The first thing…<br>After…<br>Afterwards…<br>By this stage…<br>Then…<br>All in all,…<br>",
